# Google Managed SSL with Cloudflare and Google Load Balancer – Resolution Guide

## Objective

Configure a Google Managed SSL Certificate for services.answerflow-ai.com hosted behind a Google Cloud External Application Load Balancer while DNS is managed by Cloudflare.

## Initial Problem

The Google Managed SSL Certificate remained in:

FAILED_NOT_VISIBLE

even though the Load Balancer and HTTPS frontend were configured.

DNS lookup initially returned Cloudflare proxy addresses:

104.21.x.x
172.67.x.x
2606:4700:xxxx

instead of the Google Load Balancer IP:

8.232.140.211

As a result, Google Certificate Manager could not verify domain ownership and failed certificate provisioning.

## Root Cause

The Cloudflare DNS record for services.answerflow-ai.com was configured as:

Proxy Status = Proxied (Orange Cloud)

When Cloudflare proxy is enabled, DNS queries return Cloudflare edge IP addresses rather than the actual Google Load Balancer IP. Google Managed Certificates require direct visibility of the Load Balancer endpoint during domain validation.

## Resolution Steps

### Step 1 – Verify Load Balancer IP

Identify the public IP assigned to the Google Load Balancer.

Example:

8.232.140.211

### Step 2 – Configure Cloudflare DNS

Navigate to:

Cloudflare → DNS → Records

Create or update:

Type: A
Name: services
Content: 8.232.140.211

### Step 3 – Disable Proxy

Change:

Proxied (Orange Cloud)

to:

DNS Only (Gray Cloud)

This allows public DNS resolvers to see the actual Google Load Balancer IP.

### Step 4 – Validate DNS

Execute:

nslookup services.answerflow-ai.com 1.1.1.1

Expected result:

Name: services.answerflow-ai.com
Address: 8.232.140.211

This confirms that DNS propagation is correct and publicly visible.

### Step 5 – Monitor Certificate Status

Navigate to:

Google Cloud Console
→ Load Balancing
→ SSL Certificates
→ Certificate Details

Possible states:

PROVISIONING – Google is validating and issuing the certificate.

ACTIVE – Certificate issued successfully.

FAILED_NOT_VISIBLE – Domain could not be validated.

### Step 6 – Wait for Revalidation

After DNS correction, allow Google time to revalidate.

Typical timings:

15–60 minutes: Common
1–4 hours: Acceptable
Up to 24 hours: Possible

## Validation Commands

DNS Verification:

nslookup services.answerflow-ai.com 1.1.1.1

Google DNS Verification:

nslookup services.answerflow-ai.com 8.8.8.8

Quad9 Verification:

nslookup services.answerflow-ai.com 9.9.9.9

All should resolve to:

8.232.140.211

## Key Learning

When using Google Managed SSL behind Cloudflare, domain validation requires the DNS record to be temporarily configured as DNS Only (Gray Cloud). Once the certificate becomes ACTIVE, Cloudflare Proxy (Orange Cloud) may be re-enabled if desired for CDN and DDoS protection.

## Current Status

Load Balancer: Configured
DNS Resolution: Correct (8.232.140.211)
Certificate: PROVISIONING
Domain Validation Status: Previously FAILED_NOT_VISIBLE due to Cloudflare Proxy
Expected Outcome: Certificate transitions to ACTIVE after Google revalidation.
